# python3, toolchain gnu
### --with-lto puts a bare -flto in CONFIGURE_LDFLAGS_NODIST: gcc, which finds no jobserver in the link
### commands, runs the LTRANS jobs one at a time ("lto-wrapper: warning: using serial compilation of
### <n> LTRANS jobs"). LDFLAGS_NODIST follows it on the link command lines and gives the job count of
### the framework (a link without LTO objects ignores it; clang takes no number, lld has --thinlto-jobs)
PKG_MAKEVARS+=" LDFLAGS_NODIST=-flto=${LTOPROCS}"
